<title>TURKEY: Turkey raises tax on sugar imports to 135 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkey raises tax on sugar imports to 135 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey raised customs tax on sugar imports to 135 percent from 100 percent in an effort to curb sugar imports after a rise in the 1996/97 sugar harvest and an expected bumper harvest for the next year, the Official Gazette said.  </p>
<p>It said the ruling would take immediate effect, but did not give other details.</p>
<p>Turkey's 1996/97 sugar output is seen at 1.85 million tonnes, up from 1.5 million tonnes a year ago. Beet producers expect the 1997/98 production to be about 2.05 million tonnes.</p>
<p>--Ankara newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
